WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.080
Homer Simpson isn't just a cartoon character.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.800
He is, officially, one of the most influential
people of the modern era.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.120
And he's also a pretty horrible human being.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.800
For over 30 years, Homer's been abusing his
kids, lying to his wife, and causing all kinds

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.780
of mayhem as a result.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.140
Hey, we love the guy, but the citizens of
Springfield probably lost their affection

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.830
for Homer Simpson long ago.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.500
Especially after he did all these things.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.460
The Maude mishap

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:33.180
Maude Flanders' demise via T-shirt cannon
is arguably the most shocking and callous

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.300
end in The Simpsons' long and storied history.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.280
In "Alone Again, Natura-Diddily," the Flanders
and Simpsons families visit the local racetrack,

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.100
and Homer becomes obsessed with the cheerleaders'
T-shirt cannons.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:45.760
Like, really obsessed.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.210
First, he takes off his own shirt, trying
to get the cheerleaders' attention.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.620
Next, he paints a bull's-eye on his chest.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:55.460
Given Homer's size, that would be an easy
target — and the cheerleaders let a barrage

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:56.900
of T-shirts fly straight at him.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.180
And then...

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.130
And that's the end of the line for poor Maude,
who didn't do anything wrong aside from crossing

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:09.020
paths with Homer Simpson one too many times.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:10.680
Celebrity send-off

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.580
Technically, The Simpsons' annual Treehouse
of Horror episodes aren't canonical, which

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.810
gives the show's writers plenty of room to
stretch their creative muscles and go crazy.

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:25.100
But even by normal standards, the 2009 Treehouse
of Horror segment "How to Get Ahead in Gone-Vertising"

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.180
is extra-creepy.

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:30.980
The episode begins as a Mad Men parody but
quickly descends into a dark story in which

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.100
Homer hunts down superstars for money.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.940
Homer starts by accidentally pushing Krusty
the Clown into a woodchipper.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:41.460
And then he accepts money from advertising
executives to drown George Clooney in cement,

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:45.790
to strangle Prince with his own guitar, and
to brain Neil Armstrong with a golf club.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.760
If only Homer's non-imaginary adventures weren't
also totally nuts...

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:51.500
Framing Marge

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.910
If you ask die-hard Simpsons fans to recommend
Homer's overall lowest moment, most of them

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:00.940
will probably point you to "Co-Dependent's
Day," a Season 15 episode that chronicles

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.540
Marge's struggle with alcoholism.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:06.080
Homer, of course, has been a beer-guzzling
booze hound since the very beginning.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.700
But in "Co-Dependent's Day," he enables Marge's
addiction.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.049
First he takes her to Moe's, then they go
to an Oktoberfest celebration.

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:14.659
But the worst moment?

00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:18.299
That comes when Homer, plastered from the
beer festival, tries to drive home and ends

00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:19.680
up flipping the car.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.420
When the police arrive, he frames Marge, who's
even more drunk than he is.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.120
Marge goes to jail for driving under the influence,
and later checks into a rehab facility.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.310
Homer, meanwhile, doesn't face a single consequence.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:33.360
Now that's Homer's style of justice.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:34.960
Vegas vows

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:39.960
As the saying goes, "What happens in Vegas,
stays in Vegas"— unless you're Homer Simpson.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:45.319
In the episode "Viva Ned Flanders" Homer takes
Ned to Vegas for a night of crazy fun.

00:02:45.319 --> 00:02:48.970
When they wake up from their booze-soaked
all-nighter, they're married to their waitresses

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:49.860
from the night before.

00:02:50.049 --> 00:02:54.140
So they flee back to Springfield and forget
about their second wives...for about three

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:54.780
seasons.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:58.959
In "Brawl in the Family," the two cocktail
waitresses track down their husbands.

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:03.700
After a judge refuses to annul Homer's marriage
to Amber, he takes matters into his own hands

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.800
and gets the woman drunk.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.600
When Amber wakes up, she's married to Homer's
dad.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:11.180
Horrified Amber takes off for Vegas as soon
as possible.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:15.980
It's a funny way to turn the tables...until
you actually think about it for, like, two

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:16.560
seconds.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.060
That's pretty creepy, Homer.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:18.820
Kidney failure

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.239
In the Season 10 episode "Kidney Trouble,"
we all learn a valuable lesson: Homer's an

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.940
even bigger jerk than we thought.

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:30.030
In the first half of the episode, Homer causes
his dad Abe's kidneys to explode...because

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.420
he doesn't want to stop to let him use the
bathroom.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.960
The doctor tells Abe he's a goner without
a transplant, and fortunately, Homer is an

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:36.840
exact match.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.360
Less fortunately...well, it's Homer.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:43.400
While Homer agrees to donate a kidney, he
takes off just before the surgery, leaving

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.000
his father alone and in pain.

00:03:45.469 --> 00:03:49.540
Abe only gets the life-saving organ he needs
after Homer gets hit by a car and knocked

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.800
unconscious, giving Doctor Hibbert time to
steal Homer's kidney and complete the procedure.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:55.640
Homer the henchman

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:59.820
Homer Simpson has had many, many jobs, but
he's only been good at one.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.280
Unfortunately, that happened to be when he
was working for Hank Scorpio, a straight-up

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:04.780
supervillain.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:09.340
This is Homer we're talking about, of course,
and he doesn't ever actually notice that Scorpio

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.040
is really a criminal mastermind.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.760
He's too busy doing literally anything else
to realize that he's helping Scorpio conquer

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:16.280
the world.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.220
"I'm having some trouble with the government."

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:21.780
"Awww… those jerks always walking over the
small businessman."

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:26.350
Even worse, Homer doesn't notice that his
family is absolutely miserable in Scorpio's

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.400
compound until it's too late.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.590
Eventually, he comes around, and Scorpio lets
Homer return to Springfield — but not before

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:35.560
Scorpio's forces manage to conquer the East
Coast.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:36.600
Good job, Homer.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:38.100
They couldn't have done it without you.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.480
Neighborly wish

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:44.240
Homer has gone out of his way to make Flanders'
life miserable plenty of times, but what he

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:48.140
does in the Season 3 episode "When Flanders
Failed" might take the cake.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.740
At a backyard barbecue, Flanders announces
that he's quitting his job to open his own

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:53.760
store, the Leftorium.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.220
So, naturally, Homer uses the powers of a
wishbone — to wish for Ned's business to

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:58.720
fail.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:00.020
It works.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.220
The Leftorium goes out of business, Ned's
house is repossessed, and the Flanderses are

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.400
forced to move into their car.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:09.680
Sure, Homer eventually saves Ned from bankruptcy,
but Ned never would've been in trouble in

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.760
the first place if Homer hadn't been such
a jerk.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.140
But that's Homer for ya!

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:17.660
"When he's least expecting it, bash his head
in with a chair."

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:18.480
Thanks for watching!

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:21.020
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:23.660
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

